<Lab
  title="Disclaimer | Txchyon"
  description="Txchyon is research and software, not investment advice. Read the risk disclosure and affiliate link disclosure."
  canonical="/disclaimer"
>
  <section class="lab-section first">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="lead">Please read this before using anything from Txchyon.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section tight prose">
    <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
    <p>
      Txchyon publishes research, educational content and software. We are not financial advisors, brokers or registered investment
      advisors, and nothing on this site is financial advice. Crypto can lose all of its value. Never invest more than you can afford to lose.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages, mostly older articles and the <a href="/tools">tools page</a>, contain affiliate or referral links. If you use one, we
      may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. The commissions help cover hosting and development and keep the articles free. We
      only link to products we use, and we try to say so when a link is a referral link.
    </p>

    <h2>No recommendations</h2>
    <p>We do not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>tell you which cryptocurrencies to buy or sell;</li>
      <li>give price predictions or trading signals;</li>
      <li>tell you when to enter or exit a position;</li>
      <li>guarantee profits or returns, or manage anyone's money.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Software, backtests and paper trading</h2>
    <p>
      Results we publish from the Txchyon app, including backtests and paper trading, are experiments. They use historical or simulated
      conditions, may not reflect real fees, slippage or outages, and do not predict future results. Some strategies we test lose money.
      Nothing we publish is a recommendation to trade.
    </p>

    <h2>Risks you should understand</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Market:</b> extreme volatility, 24/7 markets, thin liquidity, manipulation.</li>
      <li><b>Technical:</b> smart contract bugs, protocol exploits, wallet failures, exchange insolvency.</li>
      <li><b>Regulatory:</b> changing rules, tax obligations, regional restrictions.</li>
      <li><b>Operational:</b> user error, phishing, lost keys, rug pulls and scams.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Do your own research. Cross-check what you read here with other sources, read the documentation and audits of anything you use,
      start with small amounts, and secure your assets with hardware wallets and two-factor authentication. Keep records for your taxes.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Crypto moves fast, so articles can go out of date. Protocols change and vulnerabilities are found. We try to be accurate but cannot
      promise that everything is current. Check official project documentation before acting.
    </p>

    <h2>No professional relationship</h2>
    <p>
      Using this site does not create a client or advisor relationship. For personal advice, speak to a qualified professional who
      understands crypto and your situation.
    </p>

    <p class="small">Last updated October 23, 2026. This disclaimer supplements our <a href="/terms">terms of service</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Lab>
